course: dictionary
lesson: 786
title: Bedclothes: the covers on a bed
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Bedclothes are the covers on a bed: the sheets, blankets, duvet or quilt, and pillowcases. The word is always plural, so we say «the bedclothes», never «a bedclothes». Think of it as a bundle of covers that belong together.
explain: Read the context to work out the meaning. «His toes are freezing, and he dreams that his bedclothes have run downstairs to the kitchen fire to get warm.» Beds have covers, and cold toes are under them. The bedclothes are the things keeping him warm in bed, so they are the covers on the bed.
explain: In stories, children hide under the bedclothes with a torch to read, or pull the bedclothes over their heads when they feel scared. Each example shows what the bedclothes are for: keeping us warm and safe in bed.
fact: Bedclothes means the covers on a bed.
fact: Bedclothes includes sheets, blankets, a duvet or quilt, and pillowcases.
fact: Bedclothes is plural only: we say «the bedclothes», not «a bedclothes».
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad knots his bedclothes into a rope to climb out of a window, but that is a story, and it is very dangerous in real life.
exercise: «His toes are freezing, and he dreams that his bedclothes have run downstairs to the kitchen fire.» What are bedclothes? | Shoes and socks for cold feet | Clothes you wear to bed, like pyjamas | *The covers on a bed, such as sheets and blankets | The furniture in a bedroom
exercise: Which of these is part of the bedclothes? | A toothbrush | A football | *A pillowcase | A bookshelf
exercise: A child hides under the bedclothes with a torch. What does the child do with the torch? | Washes the windows | Sweeps the floor | *Reads a book | Cooks breakfast
test: Why do children pull the bedclothes over their heads in stories? | Because it is time for breakfast | Because they are lost at school | *Because they feel scared | Because they want to wash their hair
test: Which is the correct way to write the covers on a bed? | a bedclothe | *the bedclothes | a bedclothes | the bedclothe's
exam: In «His toes are freezing, and he dreams that his bedclothes have run downstairs to the kitchen fire», why is the idea funny? | Because toes are made of bedclothes | Because bedclothes cannot run, and it is only a dream | *Because bedclothes are always kept in the kitchen | Because the kitchen fire is always cold
